Maintainer: Raydonal Ospina <raydonal@de.ufpe.br>
Description: Partitional clustering algorithms adapted to Kendall's
    two-dimensional shape space, together with a bagging ensemble
    wrapper. Provides Partitioning Around Medoids (PAM) and Ranked
    K-medoids with the intrinsic Riemannian geodesic distance, and the
    BagClust1 ensemble that stabilises partitions via bootstrap
    aggregation. Includes reproducible utilities for simulating
    Complex Bingham and Gaussian landmark data, external validation
    indices (Rand and Fowlkes-Mallows), and paired Wilcoxon tests.
    Performance-critical routines are implemented in C++ via 'Rcpp'
    and 'RcppArmadillo'. Companion to the paper by Ospina, Nascimento and Amaral (2026).
    Not yet on CRAN; developed and maintained at
    <https://github.com/raydonal/ShapeClust>.
